## The Profit Engine (Analytics Features)

The Profit Agent runs on top of Lifetimely's analytics engine — profit-focused reporting that Shopify and Amazon merchants have used for years to understand true profitability, customer lifetime value, and marketing attribution.

Profit & Loss gives merchants an automated, real-time income statement with an unparalleled level of detail into where money comes from and where it goes — including COGS, marketing spend, refunds, fees, and operating expenses. A daily P&L report, connected to stores, ad platforms, and other cost centers, is delivered straight to the merchant's inbox so they never wait for end-of-month spreadsheets.

CAC & LTV analysis answers the question every growth team argues about: are we spending too much to acquire a customer, or could we spend more to acquire more valuable ones? Lifetimely shows lifetime value and acquisition cost side by side, with predictive LTV forecasting, cohort segmentation by product, channel, or customer segment, and analysis of which products and behaviors actually drive long-term value.

Customer Journey Tracking reveals how customers really buy: repurchase rates, time between orders, RFM segmentation, and purchase patterns across first through fourth orders and beyond. Merchants use it to identify at-risk customers and act on retention opportunities before they become churn.

Attribution centralizes ad spend, revenue, CPC, and ROAS across Google Ads, Meta (Facebook and Instagram), and TikTok in one dashboard, with first-touch and last-touch attribution — so channel and budget decisions are based on profit contribution, not just revenue.

Custom Dashboards & Metrics let each role build the reporting they need — with templates for eCommerce (sales % to target, MER, AOV, contribution margin), Acquisition (new customers, CAC, NCMER, spend by channel), Retention (repeat rate, LTV, subscriptions, CRM segments), and Finance (margins, profitability, cost breakdowns). Dashboards can be scheduled to arrive by email daily, weekly, or monthly.

