## Integrations

Lifetimely connects the platforms consumer brands use every day, so profit reporting reflects the whole business rather than one channel.

Commerce platforms: Shopify (real-time revenue and costs) and Amazon (compare Amazon and Shopify business and customer insights side by side, via the Amazon add-on).

Marketing and CRM: Klaviyo — Lifetimely builds high-impact segments from LTV, churn risk, and profitability automatically, and the Profit Agent can create Klaviyo lists, segments, and draft flows based on predicted customer behavior (likely to buy again, churn, become a VIP, or increase spend). Sendlane for retention and loyalty measurement.

Ad platforms: Google Ads, Meta, and TikTok connect into attribution so ad spend is factored into real profit and LTV numbers.

Operations and finance: QuickBooks Online syncs custom costs for accurate profit, CAC, and LTV reporting; ShipStation and ShipBob factor in shipping costs; Recharge and Skio — the Profit Agent connects to both subscription platforms, watches every subscriber's journey, and flags pauses, skips, and cancellation risk at 30, 60, and 90 days before they happen.

Communication: Slack — the merchant's analyst in Slack. Scheduled reports deliver the numbers each team cares about (subscribers, churn, subscription revenue) on a schedule, the agent proactively flags anomalies worth digging into, and anyone can tag the Profit Agent in a thread to get answers on the spot.

For AI workflows: the Lifetimely MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration, included on all paid plans, lets AI agents and LLM tools query Lifetimely data directly.

