## Company

Lifetimely is built by Amp, a company that has been building eCommerce apps for Shopify since 2013. Amp was co-founded by Patrick Barnes and Cameron Priest. Cameron co-founded and led TradeGecko, the inventory and order management platform acquired by Intuit for US$100M in 2020 to expand QuickBooks. Patrick led sales at TradeGecko before founding Advocately, a customer review management platform acquired by G2 in 2019. The leadership team also includes Shefali Thompson (VP Finance & Operations, ex-KPMG/Deloitte and TradeGecko), Laura Daley (VP Marketing, previously Hero, which exited to Klarna), and Rohan Walsh (VP Design, previously Intuit and TradeGecko).

Amp's mission: give merchants the metrics, growth levers, and tools to make impactful business moves — without stitching together dozens of disconnected point solutions. Company values include customer obsession, ownership, bias for action, antifragility, and frugality.

